Pages = {563-565},
Month = {FEB},
Abstract = {This data article presents the data collected through an extensive
   research work conducted in urban areas in the city of Athens (Greece)
   during the period 2010-2012. Data concerns 2287 questionnaires and
   microclimatic data collected through interviews to the visitors of the
   examined areas with parallel monitoring of the urban microclimatic
   characteristics. The field surveys carried out occasionally throughout
   the year covering as much as possible the different seasons under
   Mediterranean climate conditions. These data are related to the research
   articles with the titles: Seasonal differences in thermal sensation in
   the outdoor urban environment of Mediterranean climates the example of
   Athens, Greece (Tseliou et al., 2017) and Outdoor thermal sensation in a
   Mediterranean climate (Athens): The effect of selected microclimatic
   parameters (Tseliou et al., 2016). (C) 2019 The Authors. Published by
